{"content":[{"c":["PARAN"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Desert region in the northeast Sinai Peninsula west of the Arabah (Rift Valley). The settlement of Kadesh-barnea is its northernmost limit. Some scholars identify the great Et-Tih plateau of the central Sinai as a part of this wilderness."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["The wilderness of Paran is a wild, arid expanse of tableland, mountains, gorges, and wadis. The lack of water and vegetation made it a most inhospitable place and a stark contrast to the land flowing with milk and honey that was promised to Israel."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["This wilderness became the home of Ishmael (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.21.20-21","r":"Gen.21.20-21","rawR":"Gen.21.20-21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.21.20-21","value":"Gen.21.20-21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 21:20-21"},"). The nation of Israel camped there on the way from Egypt to Canaan (",{"href":"?bref=Num.10.12","r":"Num.10.12","rawR":"Num.10.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.10.12","value":"Num.10.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 10:12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.12.16","r":"Num.12.16","rawR":"Num.12.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.12.16","value":"Num.12.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:16"},"). From Kadesh-barnea, at the northern edge of the wilderness, Moses sent spies to reconnoiter the Promised Land (",{"href":"?bref=Num.13.3,26","r":"Num.13.3,26","rawR":"Num.13.3,26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.13.3,26","value":"Num.13.3,26"}],"t":"ref","v":"13:3, 26"},"). David is said to have led his band of men to this region after the death of Samuel so as to distance himself from King Saul (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.25.1","r":"1Sam.25.1","rawR":"1Sam.25.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.25.1","value":"1Sam.25.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 25:1"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Palestine_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Palestine_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Palestine_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Palestine"},"; ",{"href":"?item=SinaSinai_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"SinaSinai_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"SinaSinai_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Sina, Sinai"},"; ",{"href":"?item=WildernessWanderings_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"WildernessWanderings_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"WildernessWanderings_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Wilderness Wanderings"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Paran","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 21:20-21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.21.20-21","rawQueryValue":"Gen.21.20-21","sourceRefExact":"Gen.21.20-21"},{"anchorText":"Nm 10:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.10.12","rawQueryValue":"Num.10.12","sourceRefExact":"Num.10.12"},{"anchorText":"12:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.12.16","rawQueryValue":"Num.12.16","sourceRefExact":"Num.12.16"},{"anchorText":"13:3, 26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.13.3,26","rawQueryValue":"Num.13.3,26","sourceRefExact":"Num.13.3,26"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 25:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.25.1","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.25.1","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.25.1"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"18444983467a65d33e8dd3fa898766639c1eef90d766f1fdc7474ce19c7d4138","sourceItemName":"Paran","sourceItemOrder":36,"sourceMember":"Articles/P.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Paran","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Paran","title":"Paran","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}